--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
Bundled third-party code
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------

`fieldglass_wasm_bg.wasm` is a statically linked WebAssembly module. Every
decoder in it is pure Rust — there is no C library, no emscripten runtime and no
system dependency — which is what lets one module run in a browser with nothing
installed. The crates linked into it are listed below with the licence each is
published under. Where a crate offers a choice, the choice is the user's.

Codecs, and what reads them:

  png              0.18.1   MIT OR Apache-2.0    GRIB2 §5.41 PNG packing
  rust-j2k         0.3.0    MIT OR Apache-2.0    GRIB2 §5.40 JPEG 2000 packing
  ruzstd           0.9.1    MIT                  NetCDF-4 zstd filter (32015)
  twox-hash        2.1.3    MIT                  ruzstd's frame checksums
  flate2           1.1.9    MIT OR Apache-2.0    NetCDF-4 deflate filter, and
                                                 the zlib streams inside PNG
  miniz_oxide      0.8.9    MIT OR Zlib OR Apache-2.0   flate2's pure-Rust backend
  miniz_oxide      0.9.1    MIT OR Zlib OR Apache-2.0
  fdeflate         0.3.7    MIT OR Apache-2.0    png's fast deflate path
  adler2           2.0.1    0BSD OR MIT OR Apache-2.0   Adler-32, for zlib framing
  simd-adler32     0.3.9    MIT                  the same, vectorised
  crc32fast        1.5.0    MIT OR Apache-2.0    CRC-32, for PNG chunk integrity

Bindings and support:

  wasm-bindgen     0.2.129  MIT OR Apache-2.0    the JavaScript boundary
  wasm-bindgen-shared  0.2.129  MIT OR Apache-2.0
  unicode-ident    1.0.24   (MIT OR Apache-2.0) AND Unicode-3.0
                                                 wasm-bindgen-shared's
                                                 identifier rules
  js-sys           0.3.106  MIT OR Apache-2.0
  futures-core     0.3.32   MIT OR Apache-2.0    js-sys's promise support
  futures-task     0.3.32   MIT OR Apache-2.0
  futures-util     0.3.32   MIT OR Apache-2.0
  pin-project-lite 0.2.17   Apache-2.0 OR MIT
  slab             0.4.12   MIT
  serde-wasm-bindgen  0.6.5 MIT                  values across that boundary
  serde            1.0.229  MIT OR Apache-2.0
  serde_core       1.0.229  MIT OR Apache-2.0
  thiserror        2.0.21   MIT OR Apache-2.0    error types
  bitflags         2.11.0   MIT OR Apache-2.0
  once_cell        1.21.4   MIT OR Apache-2.0
  cfg-if           1.0.4    MIT OR Apache-2.0

The `full/` entry (`@fieldglass/wasm/full`) is the same module built with the
fetch planner and Zarr stores, and links these as well:

  serde_json       1.0.154  MIT OR Apache-2.0    Zarr metadata and the
                                                 planner's queries
  itoa             1.0.18   MIT OR Apache-2.0    serde_json's integer output
  zmij             1.0.21   MIT                  serde_json's float output
  memchr           2.8.0    Unlicense OR MIT     serde_json's string scanning

The Fieldglass crates themselves — `fieldglass`, `fieldglass-core`,
`fieldglass-grib1`, `fieldglass-grib2`, `fieldglass-netcdf`, and
`fieldglass-aec`, which decodes GRIB2 §5.42 CCSDS / AEC packing, and in the
`full/` entry `fieldglass-fetchplan` and `fieldglass-zarr`, whose blosc, LZ4
and BloscLZ decoders are written in Rust here — are part of this project and
carry the same MIT OR Apache-2.0 terms as the package.

This list is generated from the module's own dependency graph
(`cargo tree -p fieldglass-wasm --target wasm32-unknown-unknown
-e normal,no-proc-macro`, and with `--features fetchplan,zarr` for the `full/`
entry) and is regenerated when that graph changes. `cargo deny check` holds
the whole workspace to an allowed-license set on every pull request, so a crate
whose terms this project cannot ship never reaches a release.

